{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-80174",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, notice that we can factor out a $(-5)$ from each of the terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}100+40y-5{y}^{2} & =-5({y}^{2}-8y-20) & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we just need to factor the polynomial ${y}^{2}-8y-20$ in parentheses.\n\nWe start by listing the factor pairs of the constant term $(-20).$ The constant term is negative, so that means one of the factors is negative and the other is positive:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & \\times (-20) \\\\ (-1) & \\times 20 \\\\ 2 & \\times (-10) \\\\ (-2) & \\times 10 \\\\ 4 & \\times (-5) \\\\ (-4) & \\times 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find which factor pair adds up to the coefficient of the linear term $(-8):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+(-20) & =-19 & \\times  \\\\ -1+20 & =19 & \\times  \\\\ 2+(-10) & =-8 & ✓ \\\\ -2+10 & =8 & \\times  \\\\ 4+(-5) & =-1 & \\times  \\\\ -4+5 & =1 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the factor pair identified above, we write the linear term as $-8y=2y-10y$ and then factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5({y}^{2}-8y-20) & = \\\\ -5({y}^{2}+2y-10y-20) & = \\\\ -5(({y}^{2}+2y)+(-10y-20)) & = \\\\ -5(y(y+2)-10(y+2)) & = \\\\ -5(y-10)(y+2) & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-80174\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p>First, notice that we can factor out a <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"32\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c28\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2212\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c35\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c29\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> from each of the terms:</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" display=\"true\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"33\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math display=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"margin-left: 0px; margin-right: 0px;\"><mjx-mtable style=\"min-width: 17.917em;\"><mjx-table><mjx-itable><mjx-mtr><mjx-mtd style=\"text-align: right; padding-right: 0px;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2B\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c34\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D466 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2212\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c35\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-msup><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D466 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.413em;\"><mjx-